 name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1029937A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit> </non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOBE STEEL LTD</name><address><country>JP</country> </address> </addressbook> </applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO KATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEKI YUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUGIZAKI YASUAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YANAGAWA MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KABUSHIKI KAISHA KOBE SEIKO SHO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO, KATSUSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEKI, YUICHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUGIZAKI, YASUAKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YANAGAWA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO KATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEKI YUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUGIZAKI YASUAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YANAGAWA MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO, KATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEKI, YUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUGIZAKI, YASUAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YANAGAWA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An Al-Mg-Si alloy sheet having higher suitability for press molding (especially for deep drawing, protruding, and bending) than conventional JIS 6000 Al-Mg-Si alloy sheets, characterized by having such a texture that the density of the alloy in at least the Cube direction has been regulated according to the kind of press molding to be used to thereby have improved suitability for the press molding.  For example, in order for an Al-Mg-Si alloy sheet to have enhanced suitability for deep drawing, the ratio of the alloy density in the Goss direction to that in the Cube direction (Goss/Cube) is regulated to 0.3 or lower and the crystal grain diameter is regulated to 80  mu m or smaller.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une feuille en alliage Al-Mg-Si particulièrement apte à être soumise à un moulage par pression (et en particulier à un emboutissage profond, une mise en relief, et un cintrage), par rapport aux feuilles en alliage Al-Mg-Si JIS 6000 traditionnelles. La texture de cette feuille en alliage est telle que la densité de l'alliage au moins dans le sens de Cube a été régulée en fonction du type de moulage par pression destiné à être mis en oeuvre, ce qui rend cette feuille particulièrement apte à être soumise à un moulage par pression. Par exemple, afin que cette feuille en alliage Al-Mg-Si soit particulièrement apte à être soumise à un emboutissage profond, le rapport de la densité de l'alliage dans le sens de Goss à celui dans le sens de Cube (Goss/Cube) est limité à 0,3 ou moins, le diamètre du grain cristallin étant par ailleurs inférieur ou égal à 80  mu m.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>